{"t": 33.191, "n": 43, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I made two changes to fix the six `ts-phs-proof` findings. I only ran two of the five phase test files this time.\n\n- **WUP-AC7:** `test_the_outcome_record_has_the_revision_entry_of_issue_150` in `test_spec_budget_and_moved_ids.py` now has WUP-AC7 and AC 10 in its comment. The comment says the stamp refresh belongs to the unit (row 3.5).\n- **EVS-AC7:** the five fixture files can't hold a comment, so each now has a `\"proves\": \"EVS-AC7\"` key. The check reads only `declaration_error` and `runs` from the report, so I expect it to ignore the extra key, but I haven't run the fixtures against the check.\n\nI ran `test_spec_budget_and_moved_ids.py` and `test_regeneration.py` (75 passed). I did not rerun `test_regeneration_run.py`, `test_regeneration_briefs.py` or `test_regeneration_findings.py`, because this attempt didn't touch them. The plan marks for rows 7.1–7.10 were already in place, so I left them.\n\nARTIFACT phase_note: Ran test_spec_budget_and_moved_ids.py and test_regeneration.py (75 passed); earlier attempt's runs of test_regeneration_run.py, test_regeneration_briefs.py and test_regeneration_findings.py not repeated. Added a WUP-AC7 comment to the issue-150 test. Deviation: the five fixtures each carry an extra key \"proves\": \"EVS-AC7\" so the file carries the criterion (JSON has no comments), which the row's exact content doesn't list. I haven't run the fixtures against the check. Also earlier: the third pin at test_regeneration_run.py line 305 was changed (goal says three places, row 7.2 lists two). No spec found made false.", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "9626f492-a2f2-482f-b6b9-1b4f445b002c"}
